lity), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), excellent computer skills (technical), but weak memory for numbers (attention), grumpy/uncooperative/nasty remarks (crew cooperation). No concrete incidents. Candidate C: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere (crew cooperation), quick correct decisions (decision quality), understands complicated technology (technical competence), excellent attention skills (attention), but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). So both have some concerns. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is vital; C's positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite communication difficulty. B's crew cooperation concerns are more severe (nasty remarks). Also B's weak memory for numbers is a safety issue. C's lack of willingness to further education may affect adaptability but could be mitigated. So likely C is stronger overall. Emily should update vote to C.\n\nThus we will produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I agree with James and Sarah, note the technical competence confirmation, and shift my vote to Candidate C, explaining why C's strengths outweigh B's concerns.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
